                "primary_text": "<h3>Participation in a study on Human Visual recognition</h3><br/>",
                "secondary_text": "<header></header><section><b>Project Objectives</b><p>In this study, you will classify images into one of 10 categories. Each image will be presented across a few steps with <b>gradually increasing clarity</b>.</p></section><hr><section><b>Your Task & Earnings</b><p>Your total payment consists of two parts:</p><ul><li><b>Fixed Payment:</b> Based on an hourly rate of \u00a3(CHECK) (estimated duration: 12 minutes \u2192 \u00a3(CHECK) total, calculated using the median completion time).</li><li><b>Performance Bonus:</b> Earned by classifying images correctly <i>and</i> reporting your confidence accurately.</li></ul><p><b>How the bonus works:</b> Being right with high confidence maximizes your reward. However, guessing incorrectly while claiming high confidence results in a severe penalty. If you are unsure, it is safer to report low confidence for a smaller, baseline reward rather than risking an overconfident error.</p></section><hr><section><b>Requirements & Participation</b><p><b>Color Vision:</b> This task requires distinguishing photographs of objects. You must have normal color vision (as you indicated to Prolific).</p><p><b>Right to Withdraw:</b> Participation is entirely voluntary. You may stop at any time without penalty, though you must complete the survey to receive your payment. To withdraw or ask questions, contact Felipe Torres Figueroa at <a href='mailto:felipe.torres_figueroa@imt-bs.eu'>felipe.torres_figueroa@imt-bs.eu</a>.</p></section><hr><section><b>Privacy & Data Protection</b><p>Data is collected by Felipe Torres for academic research on human performance. Recipients include Felipe Torres and Nicolas Soulie. Data will be stored securely for five years post-publication (expected 2027). You have the right to access, correct, or restrict your data by contacting <a href='mailto:felipe.torres_figueroa@imt-bs.eu'>felipe.torres_figueroa@imt-bs.eu</a>. Legal basis: your consent.</p></section><hr><section><b>Consent</b><p>By proceeding, you confirm that you meet the color vision requirements, understand the terms, and consent to participate in this study.</p></section><section><b>Consent</b></section>",
                "answers": [
                    "I have read and understand the information contained in this document, and I freely and knowingly consent to participate to this research project. I also confirm that I am not colorblind, as I have indicated on my Prolific profile.",
                    "I do not consent to participate to this research project or I am colorblind."
                ]
            }
        ],
